| **#** | **Subniche**                          | **Why It’s Popular**                                                                                     | **Target Audience**                          |
|-------|---------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| **1** | **Career Paths in the Merchant Navy**  | Explains roles (e.g., Deck Officer, Engineer, Chief Mate), progression, and salary trends.             | Students, career changers, job seekers.      |
| **2** | **STCW Compliance & Certifications**  | Detailed breakdown of STCW requirements, renewal processes, and required exams (e.g., Proficiency in Survival). | Aspiring officers, training centers.        |
| **3** | **Maritime Safety & Emergency Procedures** | Focus on fire safety, man-overboard drills, medical emergencies, and AIS/AISAT training.          | Crew members, safety officers.              |
| **4** | **Navigation & Chart Reading**        | Advanced topics like electronic charts, GPS/radar basics, and collision avoidance rules.               | Deck officers, cadets.                     |
| **5** | **Engineering Basics for Crew**       | Simplified explanations of ship engines, fuel systems, and troubleshooting (for non-engineers).       | Crew members, officers.                     |
| **6** | **Offshore & Deep-Sea Operations**    | Specialized content for remote areas (e.g., Arctic shipping, oil rigs, LNG carriers).               | Offshore crew, specialized training.        |
| **7** | **Maritime Law & Legal Issues**       | Contracts (e.g., Seafarers’ Agreement), liability, and maritime jurisdiction.                          | Lawyers, shipowners, crew.                  |
| **8** | **Environmental Regulations (MARPOL, SOLAS)** | How these laws impact ship operations, pollution prevention, and compliance.                          | Environmental officers, eco-conscious crews.|
| **9** | **Digital Navigation & ECDIS Training** | Deep dive into Electronic Chart Display and Information Systems (ECDIS) requirements.                  | Modern ship crews.                           |
| **10** | **Maritime History & Cultural Impact** | How the merchant navy shaped global trade, slavery, and modern economies.                          | History buffs, educators.                  |
| **11** | **Maritime Health & Mental Wellbeing** | Stress management, crew fatigue, and mental health resources for seafarers.                          | Crew welfare programs.                       |
| **12** | **Automation & AI in Shipping**       | How AI is used in cargo tracking, autonomous ships, and predictive maintenance.                       | Tech-savvy maritime professionals.          |
| **13** | **Port Operations & Logistics**       | Behind-the-scenes of cargo handling, customs, and port security.                                   | Logistics students, port workers.           |
